Splattie - third-party components and licenses

This project bundles or depends on the following components under their own
licenses. The MIT license covers only the Splattie-original code.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LAM (Large Avatar Model)
  Source: https://github.com/aigc3d/LAM
  License: see https://github.com/aigc3d/LAM/blob/main/LICENSE
  Used as: git submodule at backend/vendor/LAM
  Notes: LAM is research code. Check the upstream license before commercial use.

FLAME (Faces Learned with an Articulated Model and Expressions)
  Source: https://flame.is.tue.mpg.de
  License: Non-commercial research license. Requires attribution.
  Used as: model files downloaded by backend/scripts/setup-gpu.sh
  Notes: Commercial use requires a separate agreement with MPI for
  Intelligent Systems. The FLAME 2023 model is loaded by LAM.

diff-gaussian-rasterization (INRIA)
  Source: https://github.com/graphdeco-inria/diff-gaussian-rasterization
  License: Non-commercial. See upstream LICENSE.
  Used as: pip dependency of LAM (CUDA extension)
  Notes: Replace with gsplat (Apache 2.0) for commercial use.

Spark 2.0
  Source: https://github.com/sparkjsdev/spark
  License: MIT
  Used as: npm dependency (@sparkjsdev/spark)

Three.js
  Source: https://threejs.org
  License: MIT
  Used as: npm dependency

JSZip
  Source: https://stuk.github.io/jszip
  License: MIT or GPL v3
  Used as: npm dependency

Demo portraits
  Source: https://www.pexels.com
  License: Pexels (free, no attribution required, attribution included anyway)
  Located in: apps/web/public/demos/
  Photographers: Shiny Diamond, TUBARONES PHOTOGRAPHY, ShotPot,
  Tima Miroshnichenko (x2), Daniel Hoffman Jackson
